# Session store isolation

Cursor and Claude are separate products with separate session files. A delete, wipe, hide, archive, or "leave no trace" request applies **only** to the product the user named. The store lists and look-alike signals that are not permission (same title, registry association, export ledger id): `~/.agents/kb/_shared/How-to-keep-session-stores-isolated.md`.

Alter another product's files only when the user names that product (Cursor, Claude, Claude Desktop, `~/.claude`, Codex, or that session id) in the same order. If the user named one product and you think the other copy should go too, **stop and ask**.
